WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.087
Triage asks one question: what
authority does this task need?

2
00:00:04.087 --> 00:00:08.938
Not who received it, not how urgent the
caller sounds, and not how senior they are.

3
00:00:08.938 --> 00:00:12.366
The checks run in a fixed order,
and the first match wins,

4
00:00:12.366 --> 00:00:17.546
so the dangerous cases are caught first:
anything claiming to come from Microsoft,

5
00:00:17.546 --> 00:00:19.984
and any target that holds an admin role,

6
00:00:19.984 --> 00:00:25.088
because a role that can reset ordinary
users can't safely reset an administrator.

7
00:00:25.088 --> 00:00:27.087
One rule deserves emphasis.

8
00:00:27.087 --> 00:00:31.587
Nothing is approved from an email,
even a convincing one from Microsoft.

9
00:00:31.587 --> 00:00:34.824
A sender address is a
quick filter, not proof.

10
00:00:34.824 --> 00:00:39.812
The check that counts is the tenant's own
audit log, matched to an approved ticket.

11
00:00:39.812 --> 00:00:42.530
Next, what automation can actually carry.
